cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite the associated article. Where the data or the
  code are used directly, please also cite the Zenodo dataset (DOI below) and
  this software repository.
title: "HRes_ETa_SAFER_Aconcagua: a Google Earth Engine workflow for high-resolution SAFER evapotranspiration mapping"
abstract: >-
  Automated, cloud-based framework implemented in Google Earth Engine to estimate
  actual evapotranspiration (ETa) at 30 m spatial resolution over the Aconcagua
  River Basin, Chile. The workflow applies the SAFER (Simple Algorithm for
  Evapotranspiration Retrieving) algorithm with fixed, historically calibrated
  coefficients to Landsat 8/9 Collection 2 Level-2 surface reflectance and surface
  temperature, combined with ERA5-Land daily reference evapotranspiration
  (FAO-56 Penman-Monteith), and includes a gap-filling strategy for
  cloud-affected months. The resulting high-resolution maps support the
  assessment of structural water stress in semi-arid agricultural basins.
